# bao1x_demo.resc -- minimum-viable Renode script for the REAL
# Baochip-1x platform (renode/bao1x.repl), booting
# build-renode/baoregon-renode-demo.elf at the real, corrected ReRAM
# base address (0x60000000 -- see docs/baochip-1x-memory-map-findings.md
# and commit 144dd81), instead of Xous's kernel.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#   renode renode/bao1x_demo.resc
#
# Real console output appears directly in Renode's monitor window via
# the duart PythonPeripheral model's stdout write (see
# renode/duart_console.repl) -- confirmed real, live "heartbeat: frame=N"
# lines incrementing continuously (baoregon-trail issue #2's MVP-demo
# bar: real, visible output, not just scoping).
#
# This just starts emulation and leaves it running -- for a bounded,
# scripted verification run (e.g. in CI or a quick smoke test), wrap
# the whole invocation in a shell `timeout`, e.g.:
#   timeout 10 renode --console --disable-xwt renode/bao1x_demo.resc

using sysbus

mach create "bao1x"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/bao1x.repl

sysbus LoadELF @build-renode/baoregon-renode-demo.elf

start
